meta {
  name: speech-to-text status
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/stt/status
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  The live state of speech-to-text, probed on every call: the pinned whisper model (presence, bytes), the whisper-cli binary with a per-platform install hint (a sentence, never a button), download progress, the configured provider and language, the route a recording would take right now and whether that route can run (speechWorks).
  
  Fence: host+origin — Loopback fence plus Origin check: an Origin header, if present, must be loopback. REST clients send no Origin header, which counts as safe — requests pass. A manually added foreign Origin answers a blank 404.
  
  Writes state: no
}
